Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["VdP cu\[AAcute]ntico forzado: Fock, FLS y representaci\[OAcute]n de \
fase", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"1e57f276-19b5-4e42-98d0-f25c52da6802"],

Cell["\<\
Igual que vdp_sin_forzamiento.nb, con un forzamiento \[ScriptCapitalE] cos(\
\[CapitalOmega]t)(a + a\[Dagger]). Ganancia de un fon\[OAcute]n (\[Kappa]p) y \
p\[EAcute]rdida de dos (\[Kappa]m), con el convenio de las notas: \[HBar] = 1 \
y disipador D[L]\[Rho] = L\[Rho]L\[Dagger] \[Minus] (L\[Dagger]L\[Rho] + \
\[Rho]L\[Dagger]L)/2. Ojo: en Mathematica E es el n\[UAcute]mero e, as\
\[IAcute] que la amplitud se escribe \[ScriptCapitalE].\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"54d5646b-9e54-5946-878f-cf314bba2c73"],

Cell["\<\
Todo est\[AAcute] en el marco que gira con el forzamiento: H = \
\[CapitalDelta] a\[Dagger]a + (\[ScriptCapitalE]/2)(a + a\[Dagger]), con \
\[CapitalDelta] = \[Omega] \[Minus] \[CapitalOmega] y la aproximaci\[OAcute]n \
de onda rotante. En el sistema de laboratorio H depende del tiempo y no hay \
estado estacionario (es peri\[OAcute]dico), as\[IAcute] que no se puede usar \
aqu\[IAcute]. Los disipadores no cambian al girar.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbe94b81-2762-3245-94f7-17681e1b6408"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["0. Cargar el paquete", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"36219bde-255f-c74c-8d84-fc2ef4fcdfd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Get", "[", 
  RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", 
     " ", "\"\<RepresentacionFase.wl\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c8a1ff56-cb6f-8a4d-95eb-f67c1a343cd3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Kappa]p", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Kappa]m", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalE]", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cb222e48-8f48-ff43-b629-98cf2fb15d6a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Lo que se elige: niveles, hamiltoniano y saltos", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b81459e0-f5fe-3a4e-9863-4156e0065d09"],

Cell["\<\
Igual que en el cuaderno sin forzamiento. Con d \[GreaterEqual] 4 la soluci\
\[OAcute]n simb\[OAcute]lica crece mucho: conviene dar valores \
num\[EAcute]ricos a los par\[AAcute]metros antes de llamar a \
estadoEstacionario.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2fd10339-c301-df47-a3fe-cafaa88d1dd7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"d", " ", "=", " ", "3"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"H", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ad", " ", "**", " ", "a"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalE]", "/", "2"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"a", " ", "+", " ", "ad"}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"saltos", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Kappa]p", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"+", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Kappa]m", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:=",ExpressionUUID->"090434b7-f1aa-7247-afd0-63654905feab"],

